# gdlint configuration.
#
# Godot reports GDScript warnings only inside the editor — a headless run prints
# nothing — so this is the repo's static check. The rules kept below are the ones
# that catch real problems (dead arguments, tautological comparisons, mixed
# indentation, naming). The disabled ones are stylistic rules that conflict with
# how these demos are written on purpose:
#
#   class-definitions-order  Demos order declarations to read top-to-bottom as a
#                            lesson, not to satisfy a canonical section order.
#   max-line-length          Aligned tables of constants, and the Transform3D /
#                            Vector3 expressions that only make sense read as
#                            one line, wrap badly.
#   function-variable-name   Tests declare local ALL_CAPS fixtures (STEP,
#                            FORWARD) to mirror the constant they stand for.
#   no-else-return /         Explicit symmetrical branches are clearer than the
#   no-elif-return /         early-return rewrites in teaching code.
#   max-returns
#
# gdformat is deliberately NOT run over this repo: it collapses the hand-aligned
# constant tables that make the demos readable, and it reformatted almost every
# file in the 2D collection when it was tried there. Indentation consistency is
# covered by mixed-tabs-and-spaces instead.
disable:
  - class-definitions-order
  - max-line-length
  - function-variable-name
  - no-else-return
  - no-elif-return
  - max-returns
